  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe Heidenhain DIN/ISO post (`assets/posts/heidenhain.cps`) wrote `Q395` in G200 and `Q208`/`Q395` in G205 for each control. These words are not in the cycle 200/205 parameter set of iTNC 530 340 49x software (the Fehlmann Picomax 55 has NC 340490-03).\n\nVersion sources (`docs/research/heidenhain/`):\n\n- `differences.md` B2, row \"Cycle 205 (UNIVERSAL PECKING) Q list\": Q379/Q253 from iTNC 340 422; Q208/Q395 only from iTNC 60642x-04, TNC 640 34059x-04, TNC 620 81760x-01, TNC 320 77185x-01. Source: \"Cycle 205: Input parameter Q208 for retraction feed rate added\" (670388-25 p13).\n- `differences.md` B2, row \"Cycle 200 (DRILLING) Q list\": Q395 from the same versions.\n- `differences.md` B3: the cycle 200/205 example blocks of the 340 49x manuals end without Q395/Q208 (for example 53318820 p237 and p262).\n- `dialects.md`: profiles `itnc-49x` (c200 `q211`, c205 `q379`) and `itnc-60642x-04` (c200 `q395`, c205 `q208`, \"the only iTNC with Q395/Q208\").\n\nThe rules (helper `drillLevel()`, keyed on `machine.controllerIdentity`, structured so that the resolver of #4095 can replace it):\n\n- **One guard for the NC software string (#4172 review).** The post parses the complete canonical identifier of `dialects.md` section 1: `^\\d{5}\\d-\\d{2}( SP[1-9]\\d{0,2})?$` (6 digits, `-`, exactly 2 release digits, optional ` SP<n>`, nothing else). The first five digits are the family, the sixth is the variant. Then one table row must match the model, the family, the variant range and a release that the research names. Release `-00` is never valid. Each other string with a stated identity is refused by name.\n- Variant ranges: iTNC 530 34049 + `0..4` and 60642 + `0..5` (`dialects.md`); 340 422 only (family 34042, variant 2); TNC 640/620/320 families `0..5` (the research gives no range for them; a higher variant is refused).\n- Level `q379`: G200 without `Q395`; G205 with `Q379`/`Q253`, without `Q208` and `Q395`. For iTNC 530 340 422 (each release `-01` to `-99`; the research names none), 34049x-01 to -08, 60642x-01 to -03; TNC 640 34059x-01/-02; TNC 620 34056x-01 to -04, 73498x-01/-02; TNC 320 34055x-01 to -06.\n- Level `q208` (the output of today): iTNC 530 60642x-04 (also with ` SP<n>`); TNC 640 34059x-04 to -11 and -16 to -18; TNC 620 81760x-01 to -08 and -16 to -18; TNC 320 77185x-01, -02, -04 to -06 and -18. A release that the research does not name (for example TNC 640 -03 or -12) is refused.\n- A stated control or version that is not in the table: G200/G205 are refused by name (\"the cycle 200/205 parameter set of <model> NC <nc> is not known to this post - refused, not posted\"). This follows `dialects.md`.\n- On level `q379`, the post drops `Q395` only for `Q395=0` (tool-tip reference, the only reference of the old cycle). It drops `Q208` only for the top of the range (99999.999). Each other value is refused by name (\"G205 Q208=<v> cannot be written for <model> NC <nc>: its cycle 205 has no Q208\"). The CAM does not ask for another value today.\n- No controller identity: the output of today stays. The decision file gives the reason: the failure of these words on an old control is a load-time alarm with no motion, and the words do not change the tool path. See `docs/decisions/4094-dinsio-cycle-parameter-level.md`.\n\nThe dwell (`FUNCTION DWELL` / `G04 F`) is #4093. A contributor (JSwetz) holds that issue with PR #4158. This PR does not change the dwell lines.\n\n## Readings\n\nPicomax 55 (iTNC 530 340490-03), peck hole (G205) and deep hole (G200):\n\n```\nG205 Q200=+0 Q201=-8 Q206=+150 Q202=+4 Q203=+0 Q204=+0 Q212=+0 Q205=+4 Q258=+0 Q259=+0 Q257=+4 Q256=+1 Q211=+0.2 Q379=+0 Q253=+150\nG200 Q200=+0 Q201=-8 Q206=+90 Q202=+4 Q210=+0 Q203=+0 Q204=+0 Q211=+0\n```\n\niTNC 530 606425-04: the same blocks with `Q208=+99999.999 Q395=+0` (G205) and `Q395=+0` (G200), as before.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\nNew submodule `crates/post/tests/heidenhain_cycles/levels.rs` of the existing `heidenhain_cycles` binary (no new test binary):\n\n- `picomax_340490_03_writes_g200_and_g205_without_q208_and_q395` (the shipped Picomax machine file)\n- `controls_before_the_q208_level_write_the_q379_set`\n- `controls_from_the_q208_level_keep_q208_and_q395`\n- `an_unknown_control_or_version_is_refused_by_name`\n- `a_malformed_or_unsupported_nc_identifier_is_refused_by_name` (#4172 review): `340490-03junk`, `340490-030`, `340490-3`, `340490-03 sp8`, `606425-04 SP`, `606425-04 SP0`, `606425-04SP8`, `340490-00`, `340490-09`, `606425-05`, TNC 640 `340595-12`, TNC 620 `817600-00`, `340499-03`, `340495-03`, `606426-04`, `340421-02`, and TNC 640 with `340490-03`. Outer white space is refused before, when the machine file loads.\n- The valid rows now also cover `340490-03`, `340494-05`, `606425-04 SP8`, TNC 640 `340595-11`, TNC 620 `817600-18`.\n- `a_q208_ask_the_340_49x_cycle_cannot_take_is_refused_by_name` (a script variant asks `Q208=500`)\n\nThe existing `peck_and_deep_have_distinct_documented_native_cycles_and_q_inventory` pins the output with no identity (unchanged).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. Each golden with `Q395`/`Q208` (`crates/app/tests/golden/nc/heidenhain/drill_peck.nc`, `drill_plate.nc`, `synth_heidenhain.nc`, `crates/post/tests/golden/wcs_flip/heidenhain_x.nc`) posts on a machine with no controller identity. Their output does not change.\n\n## Gate (macOS)\n\nAll results are on head `e20797ba4` (log head SHA `e20797ba437f210cf58008e0e54cbd7bbbfd509b`).\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test heidenhain_cycles`: 17 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: 220 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled. The plan includes `post suites: heidenhain_cycles`, `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`. All are ok.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: 6 steps, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nThe previous head `5c6573102` had the same results (16 tests in `heidenhain_cycles`).\n\nAn earlier Windows gate on head `434559e2c` found one red test: `levels::a_q208_ask_the_340_49x_cycle_cannot_take_is_refused_by_name` (no refusal). The cause was in the post, not in the test. The q379-level guard compared the asked Q208 with `RETRACT_FEED_MAX` itself. The script variant changed that constant, so it changed the two sides, and the guard did not fire. Commit `5c6573102` compares the ask with a fixed constant `OLD_CYCLE_RETRACT_FEED` (99999.999). The test now also asserts that its variant changes the script. The decision file records this.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No run on a real iTNC 530 340490-03 control. The user can load the G200/G205 output on the Fehlmann later.\n- The Q373 level (TNC 640/620 -16 and later, TNC 320 771851-18) and option 19 on the TNC 620 are not in scope (#4095).\n\nChangelog: Heidenhain DIN/ISO post: G200 and G205 follow the controller identity. iTNC 530 340 49x and other controls before the Q208/Q395 level get no Q395 (G200) and no Q208/Q395 (G205). An unknown control is refused by name.\n\nEffort: high\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4094\n\n",
